# Prototype System

`prototype/plugin.html` is **not hand-authored** — it is a generated file produced by patching the compiled `dist/ui.html` with a Figma mock shim. Never edit it directly; regenerate it instead.

## Sync command

```bash
npm run sync:prototype                  # full build (npm run build) then patch
npm run sync:prototype -- --no-build   # patch only — skip rebuild, use when only editing shim.js
```

### What `scripts/sync-prototype.js` does

1. Runs `npm run build` (skipped with `--no-build`)
2. Reads `dist/ui.html` (the fresh build artifact)
3. Injects `prototype/shim.js` as a `<script>` block before `</head>`
4. Wraps `<main class="scrollable-content">` … `</footer>` in `<div id="plugin-chrome">` with a simulated Figma title bar (logo base64-encoded from `assets/12.27 _ logo.png` at patch time)
5. Writes the result to `prototype/plugin.html`

## Canonical source files

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `prototype/shim.js` | **Edit this** — source of truth for mock data, postMessage handling, control panel, CSS overrides |
| `scripts/sync-prototype.js` | Patch script — reads `dist/ui.html` + `shim.js`, writes `plugin.html` |
| `prototype/plugin.html` | **Generated output — do not edit** |

## What the shim does

### `parent.postMessage` interception
Instead of a blanket no-op, the shim intercepts specific outbound messages and responds:
- `toggle-width` → resizes `#plugin-chrome`, `main`, and `footer` between 240 px ↔ 188 px (matching `figma.ui.resize`)
- `toggle-controls` → echoes back a `controls-setting` message so `ui.ts` can update controls visibility

All other outbound messages are silently dropped.

### CSS overrides (injected into `<head>`)
- `html` gets a light gray background (`#e8e8e8`)
- `body` becomes `display: flex; flex-direction: row` for side-by-side plugin + control panel layout
- `#plugin-chrome` is a 240 px wide flex column card with shadow and `border-radius: 10px`
- `#plugin-title-bar` is always white (Figma chrome convention)
- `main.scrollable-content` and `footer` use `var(--color-background-main)` so all themes paint correctly

### Mock messages (fired 300 ms after `DOMContentLoaded`)
`theme-preference`, `ui-section-states`, `selection-state`, `emoji-navigation-state`, `bookmarks`, `navigation-state`, `controls-setting`, `controls-group-settings`, `navigation-context-update`, `nudge-settings`, `update-layout-state`

### Control panel (`#ctrl-panel`)
Appended to `<body>` as a sidebar next to `#plugin-chrome`.
- **Theme** buttons: `figma-dark` / `figma-light` / `boilerplate` / `cybertron` — calls `document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', key)` directly
- **State** buttons: `Layer Selected` / `No Selection` — fires the relevant mock sandbox messages
- A `MutationObserver` on `data-theme` keeps control-panel button active states in sync when the theme is changed from the Settings panel inside the plugin

### Settings overlay
A `MutationObserver` watches `#settings-overlay` for the `open` class. When it opens, the overlay is repositioned via inline styles to match `#plugin-chrome`'s exact bounding rect, confining the modal to the card rather than the full browser viewport.

## Theme switching

The control panel and the plugin's own Settings panel both change `data-theme` on `<html>`. They stay in sync automatically via the `MutationObserver` described above. All five themes work because `prototype/plugin.html` embeds the full compiled `src/styles.css`.

## Serving locally

```bash
npx serve prototype   # or any static server pointed at the prototype/ folder
```
Then open `http://localhost:3000/plugin.html`.
